# Ground generator data (D33 step 2): recipes and the block -> recipe map for the four A2 ground sheets. Read by generator_ground_op.
#   RECIPE | name | hue 0..359 | sat 0..100 | light 0..100 | contrast 0..100 | pattern noise|cobble|plank|blades | scale 1..3 | seed
#   BLOCK  | <sheet> | <block 0..31 row-major, 8 across> | <recipe>      (blocks not listed stay transparent: nothing of the original is copied)
# The surface (texture, edge ring, colours) is generated; only the original's transparency (the autotile geometry the RPG Maker runtime cuts) is read.
# Hand-tuning: edit the WEIGHT of a slot in &.widgits/concept-bank/data/spokes/ground_<recipe>.pdl (warm, wet, wear, grain, edge); 0.0 = the recipe as written.
# The block -> recipe map reuses the D27 style choice (green = grass/foliage, sand = dirt/wood, stone = rock/tile/pits, azure = ice/water-tone, ember = lava/fire, plum = violet).
RECIPE | grass  | 108 | 40 | 34 | 26 | blades | 2 | 1101
RECIPE | dirt   | 28  | 34 | 36 | 24 | noise  | 1 | 2202
RECIPE | stone  | 222 | 7  | 46 | 30 | cobble | 1 | 3303
RECIPE | ice    | 196 | 42 | 62 | 22 | noise  | 2 | 4404
RECIPE | lava   | 12  | 72 | 38 | 34 | noise  | 1 | 5505
RECIPE | violet | 285 | 30 | 34 | 24 | noise  | 2 | 6606
